:step 1979658, :call [gate-proof-elab-have 8]}\\n273\\t     {:idx 914, :step 1980171, :call [gate-proof-elab-have-impl 8]}\\n274\\t     {:idx 915, :step 1980649, :call [gate-typing-type-of-term 3]}\\n275\\t     {:idx 916, :step 1981114, :call [gate-syntax-kind? 1]}\\n276\\t     {:idx 917, :step 1981626, :call [gate-syntax-type? 1]}\\n277\\t     {:idx 918, :step 1982138, :call [gate-syntax-variable? 1]}\\n278\\t     {:idx 919, :step 1983130, :call [gate-syntax-binder? 1]}\\n279\\t     {:idx 920, :step 1987185, :call [gate-syntax-ref? 1]}\\n280\\t     {:idx 921, :step 1990759, :call [gate-syntax-ascription? 1]}\\n281\\t     {:idx 922, :step 1994333, :call [gate-syntax-host-constant? 1]}\\n282\\t     {:idx 923, :step 1995889, :call [gate-syntax-app? 1]}\\n283\\t     {:idx 924, :step 1999015, :call [gate-typing-type-of-app 4]}\\n284\\t     {:idx 925, :step 1999493, :call [gate-typing-type-of-term 3]}\\n285\\t     {:idx 926, :step 1999958, :call [gate-syntax-kind? 1]}]\\n286\\t    ```\\n287\\t- **Progression at `4,000,000` & Completion at `5,030,283` (`8M` Trial)**:\\n288\\t  - **At `4M`**: `1,924 / 2,360` calls (`81.53%`), `pc = 180` (`[:return 0]` inside `yang.call/_descriptor`), continuation depth `48` (`{:return 48}`), inside 7th `gate-typing-rebuild-type`.\\n289\\t  - **At `8M`**: **Halts cleanly at step `5,030,283`** (`2,360` calls, `112` distinct arities) returning `[:yin.k/ok [:ok [(<a>) (Π [A ✳] (Π [B ✳] (Π [f (Π [⇧ A] B)] (Π [x A] (Π [⇧ A] B)))))]]]` (`A = B = C` exact match).\\n290\\t\\n291\\t---\\n292\\t\\n293\\t## 4. Instrumented vs Uninstrumented Results & Semantic-vs-Walker Divergence\\n294\\t\\n295\\t### 4.1 Exact Instrumentation Cost (`kernel-trace-form`)\\n296\\t\\n297\\t`kernel-trace-form` (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1839–1860`) injects `(def gate-execution-trace (stream/make 1000000))` once in setup and prepends a native `(stream/put! gate-execution-trace ['fn-sym arity])` side effect at the entry of each kernel arity body (native call — **not** a §8.10 guest call). Comparing completing runs with and without instrumentation yields exact integer step deltas:\\n298\\t\\n299\\t| Fixture & Lane | Instrumented Steps (`Setup + Exec`) | Uninstrumented Steps (`Setup + Exec`) | Total Delta (`%`) | Exact Marginal Cost per Traced Call |\\n300\\t| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\\n301\\t| `:check-accepted` × `:c-semantic` (`720` calls) | `1,207,270` (`20,715 + 1,186,555`) | `1,202,940` (`20,705 + 1,182,235`) | `+4,330` (`+0.36%`) | `+10` setup + **`6.000` steps/call** (`4,320 / 720`) |\\n302\\t| `:check-accepted` × `:c-walker` (`720` calls) | `2,086,120` (`35,707 + 2,050,413`) | `2,078,184` (`35,691 + 2,042,493`) | `+7,936` (`+0.38%`) | `+16` setup + **`11.000` steps/call** (`7,920 / 720`) |\\n303\\t| `:check-assume-have-discharge` × `:c-semantic` (`2,360` calls) | `5,030,283` (`20,824 + 5,009,459`) | `5,016,113` (`20,814 + 4,995,299`) | `+14,170` (`+0.28%`) | `+10` setup + **`6.000` steps/call** (`14,160 / 2,360`) |\\n304\\t\\n305\\t*(In the PC opcode profile of `:check-assume-have-discharge`, the `14,160` instrumentation instructions decompose into exactly `2,360 × 6`: `+4,720` `:var` [`2/call`], `+4,720` `:call` [`2/call`: `stream/put!` + `let [_ ...]` discard lambda], `+2,360` `:const` [`1/call`], and `+2,360` `:closure` [`1/call`].)*\\n306\\t\\n307\\t### 4.2 What `:c-semantic` Sees on `:check-accepted` That `:c-walker` Does Not\\n308\\t\\n309\\tBoth evaluators ingest the **exact same compiled UAST** (`215,882` AST nodes) and emit the **exact same 720-element `:executed-calls` sequence** (`#0..#719`). Neither evaluator takes a different branch or extra retry.\\n310\\t\\n311\\tThe difference is strictly **step granularity per UAST construct**:\\n312\\t- **`yin.vm.semantic/vm-hot*` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc`)**: Linearizes variable/literal operands into virtual registers. A function call `[:call rd rf [r1 ... rk] tail?]` resolves `rf` and all `k` argument registers and jumps to the target PC in **1 step**; an `if` branch `[:branch-false rtest target]` executes in **1 step**.\\n313\\t- **`yin.vm.ast-walker/cesk-transition` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc`)**: Walks the AST as a fine-grained CESK state machine:\\n314\\t  1. Entering `{:type :application}` pushes an `:eval-operator` frame (**1 step**), evaluates the operator (**≥1 step**), and pops `:eval-operator` to push `:eval-operand` (**1 step**).\\n315\\t  2. Each operand evaluates (**≥1 step**) and transitions `:eval-operand` to the next operand or final application (**1 step per operand**).\\n316\\t  3. Entering `{:type :if}` pushes `:eval-test` (**1 step**) before evaluating the test and branching (**≥2 steps**).\\n317\\t\\n318\\tBecause `:var` (`47.7%` of all semantic instructions) and `:call` (`25.4%`) dominate the program, `:c-walker` deterministically executes **`1.7280x`** transitions per `:c-semantic` instruction:\\n319\\t- At call `#692` (`[gate-syntax-ascription? 1]`), `:c-semantic` is at step `1,157,550` and finishes calls `#693..#719` (`27` NbE quotation calls returning `true` from `gate-norm-beta-eq?` and constructing `[:ok [term thm-type]]`) in `49,720` more instructions (`1,207,270` total).\\n320\\t- At that exact same call `#692`, `:c-walker` is at step `1,995,071`, exhausts `2,000,000` `4,929` steps later inside a `yang/library` call of `#693`, and never sees calls `#693..#719` (`[gate-nbe-quotation- 2]`, `[gate-syntax-binder? 1]`, `[gate-syntax-variable? 1]`, `[gate-utils-decomposer 3]`, etc.) unless given `86,120` additional steps (`2,086,120`).\\n321\\t\\n322\\t### 4.3 Bytecode PC Hotspot Profile (`:c-semantic`) — Proving the `95%+` Call-Protocol Share\\n323\\t\\n324\\tProfiling every executed PC on `:check-assume-have-discharge` (`5,009,459` execution instructions) and `:check-accepted` (`1,186,555` execution instructions) and decoding segment-0 closure entry points reveals exact integer multiples of the total §8.10 guest invocation count (**`9,598` §8.10 calls** = `8,259` non-tail `invoke` + `1,339` tail `invoke-with` in `:check-assume-have-discharge`; **`2,292` §8.10 calls** = `1,919` non-tail + `373` tail in `:check-accepted`):\\n325\\t\\n326\\t| Decoded Bytecode Owner (`PC` & Source Site) | `:check-accepted` Insts (`%` of `1.187M`) | `:check-assume-have-discharge` Insts (`%` of `5.009M`) | Exact Call-Count Formula (`N = 9,598` in `have-discharge`) |\\n327\\t| :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- |\\n328\\t| **`dsg__assoc` + `[one]`/`[two]` continuations** (`PC 21, 52`, `clojure.cljc:2147–2154`) | `215,642` (`18.17%`) | **`898,744` (`17.94%`)** | Multi-closure `(conj m (conj [] k v))` + `data/content=` `nil` checks on every invocation map, witness strip, option map, & error map |\\n329\\t| **`dsg__get`** (`PC 11`, `clojure.cljc:2144`) | `120,660` (`10.17%`) | **`504,436` (`10.07%`)** | `~52.6` insts per §8.10 call (`5` insts × `~10.5` `dsg__get` calls per invocation!) |\\n330\\t| **`yang.call/_descriptor`** (`PC 161`, `call.cljc:52–55`) | `103,140` (`8.69%`) | **`431,910` (`8.62%`)** | **`9,598 × 45`** (`15` insts × `3` calls per invocation: `1` in `eligible?`, `2` via `entry`) |\\n331\\t| **`yang.call/valid-invocation?` + `_named-pairs?`** (`call.cljc:41–84`) | `126,060` (`10.62%`) | **`527,890` (`10.54%`)** | **`9,598 × 55`** (`45` in `valid-invocation?` + `10` in `_named-pairs?` re-validating compiler-built maps) |\\n332\\t| **`call-entry` (`PC 454` + `[dsg__entry_outcome]` `PC 668`)** (`clojure.cljc:1055–1097`) | `76,917` (`6.48%`) | **`325,443` (`6.50%`)** | Shared descriptor entry wrapper checking `:clj/outcome-token`, `:yang.call/named`, and unwrapping `[:yin.k/ok v]` |\\n333\\t| **`dsg__admitted?` (`PC 441, 661, 825`) + `dsg__make_admission` (`PC 123`)** (`clojure.cljc:2095–2116`) | `73,368` (`6.18%`) | **`307,428` (`6.14%`)** | **`9,596 × 32`** (`2` calls are data-invoker lookups; every descriptor call strips `:clj/admission`, mints a fresh witness closure, and compares closures) |\\n334\\t| **`yang.call/invoke` + `[target]`/`[record]` (`PC 227, 544, 723`)** (`call.cljc:109–119`) | `65,246` (`5.50%`) | **`280,806` (`5.61%`)** | **`8,259` non-tail calls** (`8,259 × 34` insts) |\\n335\\t| **`dsg__equal`** (`PC 16`, `clojure.cljc:2145`) | `62,676` (`5.28%`) | **`263,380` (`5.26%`)** | `5` insts × `~5.5` structural `data/content=` checks per call (including closure witness comparison) |\\n336\\t| **`yang.call/eligible?` + `[descriptor]` (`PC 405, 576`)** (`call.cljc:60–64`) | `41,256` (`3.48%`) | **`172,764` (`3.45%`)** | **`9,598 × 18`** insts |\\n337\\t| **`yang.call/invocation` + `invocation-with`** (`call.cljc:86–95`) | `38,964` (`3.28%`) | **`163,166` (`3.26%`)** | Allocates 4-key / 5-key invocation record via `dsg__assoc` on every call |\\n338\\t| **`yang.call/entry`** (`PC 411`, `call.cljc:57–58`) | `27,504` (`2.32%`) | **`115,176` (`2.30%`)** | **`9,598 × 12`** (`6` insts × `2` calls per invocation) |\\n339\\t| **`dsg__empty`** (`PC 32`, `clojure.cljc:2155`) | `13,752` (`1.16%`) | **`57,588` (`1.15%`)** | **`9,598 × 6`** insts |\\n340\\t| **`yang.call/invoke-with` + `[record]` (`PC 198, 693`)** (`call.cljc:97–107`) | `9,698` (`0.82%`) | **`~34,814` (`0.69%`)** | **`1,339` tail calls** |\\n341\\t| **Subtotal — Static Prelude (`PC 0..850`) Alone** | **`974,883` (`82.16%`)** | **`4,083,545` (`81.52%`)** | Before counting per-call-site `compile-guest-call` bridges (`u/capture`, `raise` closure, arg vector, `bind-outcome`)! |\\n342\\t| **Per-Call-Site `compile-guest-call` + `bind-outcome` Bridges** | `~160,781` (`13.55%`) | **`~681,091` (`13.60%`)** | `8,259` `:current-continuation` ops, `raise` closures, `[:yin.k/ok v]` re-wrap & `bind-outcome` unwrap |\\n343\\t| **Actual `yang/library` + LaTTe Kernel Computation (Residual)** | **`~50,891` (`4.29%`)** | **`~244,823` (`4.89%`)** | Direct entry bodies of all `144` kernel `defn`s take only **`32,700` insts (`0.65%`)**; `48` library `defn` entry bodies take **`98,984` insts (`1.98%`)** |\\n344\\t\\n345\\t---\\n346\\t\\n347\\t## 5. Minimal Self-Contained Reproduction (Per-Call Cost Amplification)\\n348\\t\\n349\\tThe following minimal 2-function guest program (`0` host dependencies, `0` kernel code) reproduces the exact `14.4x – 14.9x` per-call step amplification when compiled across `yang.clojure`'s four lowering modes (`N = 0, 100, 1000` iterations to isolate exact marginal cost `(steps(1000) - steps(100)) / 900` free of setup cost):\\n350\\t\\n351\\t```clojure\\n352\\t;; Non-tail call probe (1 guest call to `callee` + 1 tail self-call per iteration;\\n353\\t;; difference vs `callee` inlined isolates 1 non-tail guest call, or see direct 1-call loop):\\n354\\t[(defn callee [x] (+ x 1))\\n355\\t (defn driver [n acc]\\n356\\t   (if (= n 0)\\n357\\t     acc\\n358\\t     (let [y (callee acc)]   ;; non-tail call (or `(callee acc)` in tail position for tail probe)\\n359\\t       (recur (- n 1) y))))\\n360\\t (driver N 0)]\\n361\\t```\\n362\\t\\n363\\t*(Note: `recur` compiles to a direct local loop closure call `dsg__loop0`, so `(let [y (callee acc)] (recur (- n 1) y))` executes **exactly `1` guest `defn` call per iteration**! For the tail-call row, `(defn step-fn [n acc] (if (= n 0) acc (step-fn (- n 1) (+ acc 1))))` executes **exactly `1` tail guest `defn` call per iteration**.)*\\n364\\t\\n365\\t### 5.1 Measured Marginal Steps per Single Guest Function Call\\n366\\t\\n367\\t| Compiler Mode (`yang/compile-program` opts) | Call Kind | `:c-semantic` Steps (`N=0 / N=100 / N=1000`) | `:c-semantic` **Steps / Call** | `:c-walker` Steps (`N=0 / N=100 / N=1000`) | `:c-walker` **Steps / Call** | Amplification vs `:arg-vector` |\\n368\\t| :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n369\\t| `nil` (raw closure, native arity) | Non-tail | `26 / 2,026 / 20,026` | **`20.0`** | `41 / 3,541 / 35,041` | **`35.0`** | `0.56x / 0.54x` |\\n370\\t| `nil` (raw closure, native arity) | Tail | `16 / 1,516 / 15,016` | **`15.0`** | `24 / 2,824 / 28,024` | **`28.0`** | `0.41x / 0.41x` |\\n371\\t| `{:calling-convention :arg-vector}` (pre-outcome) | Non-tail | `26 / 3,626 / 36,026` | **`36.0`** | `41 / 6,541 / 65,041` | **`65.0`** | **`1.00x` (baseline)** |\\n372\\t| `{:calling-convention :arg-vector}` (pre-outcome) | Tail | `34 / 3,734 / 37,034` | **`37.0`** | `57 / 6,957 / 69,057` | **`69.0`** | **`1.00x` (baseline)** |\\n373\\t| `{:outcomes true}` (§8.10 common-call, no invoker) | Non-tail | `226 / 53,026 / 528,226` | **`528.0`** | `368 / 92,168 / 918,368` | **`918.0`** | **`14.67x / 14.12x`** |\\n374\\t| `{:outcomes true}` (§8.10 common-call, no invoker) | Tail | `686 / 49,586 / 489,686` | **`489.0`** | `1,159 / 85,559 / 845,159` | **`844.0`** | **`13.22x / 12.23x`** |\\n375\\t| **`{:outcomes true, :invoker true}` (Gate Mode)** | **Non-tail** | `1,534 / 55,334 / 539,534` | **`538.0`** | `2,624 / 96,024 / 936,624` | **`934.0`** | **`14.94x / 14.37x`** |\\n376\\t| **`{:outcomes true, :invoker true}` (Gate Mode)** | **Tail** | `2,004 / 51,904 / 501,004` | **`499.0`** | `3,431 / 89,431 / 863,431` | **`860.0`** | **`13.49x / 12.46x`** |\\n377\\t\\n378\\tUnder the current gate convention (`934` walker steps/call), **a simple loop of just `2,142` non-tail guest function calls exhausts the entire `2,000,000` walker instruction budget** (`2,142 × 934 = 2,000,628`). `:check-accepted` makes `2,292` guest calls (`2.09M` walker steps), and `:check-assume-have-discharge` makes `9,598` guest calls (`~8.69M` walker steps).\\n379\\t\\n380\\t### 5.2 Exact Lowering Sites Responsible (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` & `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc`)\\n381\\t\\n382\\t1. **Per-call witness closure re-minting & structural closure comparison (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1267, 2095–2116`)**:\\n383\\t   Every call site executes `(dsg__admitted? callee)`, which reads `:yang.call/entry` and `:clj/admission`, allocates a new map `(dsg__assoc candidate :clj/admission nil)`, allocates a brand-new closure `(dsg__make_admission ...)`, and runs `(dsg__equal witness fresh-witness)` (`data/content=` recursively comparing closure payloads and captured descriptor maps). Even direct calls to top-level `defn`s defined in the same compilation unit (`gate-*` and `yang/library` helpers) pay this full dynamic authenticity check on every invocation.\\n384\\t2. **Multi-closure `dsg__assoc` implementation (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2146–2154`)**:\\n385\\t   `dsg__assoc` is a 7-arg guest lambda `(fn [m k v k2 v2 k3 v3] (let [one (conj m (conj [] k v))] (if (data/content= k2 nil) one (let [two ...] ...))))` rather than calling native `assoc` (or fixed-arity helpers), costing `~22–45` instructions per map update (`898,744` semantic instructions — `17.94%` of the entire run).\\n386\\t3. **Redundant descriptor lookup, 4-key invocation map allocation, and self-validation (`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:52–119`)**:\\n387\\t   `yang.call/invoke` calls `eligible?` (which calls `_descriptor` and `entry`, which calls `_descriptor` a second time), then calls `entry` again (`_descriptor` a third time), builds a 4-key map via 4 nested `assoc` calls (`yang.call/invocation`), and immediately runs `valid-invocation?` (`4` `contains?` + `2` `vector?` + `_named-pairs?` + `empty?`) on the map `yang.call/invocation` just constructed (`959,800` semantic instructions across `_descriptor` + `valid-invocation?` + `_named-pairs?`).\\n388\\t4. **Non-tail continuation capture + double outcome wrap/unwrap (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1072–1084, 1222–1256`)**:\\n389\\t   On every non-tail call (`8,259` calls in `:check-assume-have-discharge`), `compile-guest-call` captures the current continuation (`u/capture`) and allocates a `raise` escape closure so `yang.call/invoke` can return a bare value; inside `call-entry` (`lines 1077–1080`), the callee's `[:yin.k/ok v]` outcome is unwrapped to `v`, returned through `yang.call/invoke`, and **immediately re-wrapped** into `[:yin.k/ok v]` at `line 1232` (`(outcome-node ok-tag (u/v result))`), only for the caller's `bind-outcome` to unwrap `[:yin.k/ok v]` a second time! (Tail calls already pass `:clj/outcome-token` to forward outcomes without unwrapping; non-tail calls do not.)\\n390\\t\\n391\\t---\\n392\\t\\n393\\t## 6. Recommended Next Round\\n394\\t\\n395\\t### 6.1 Primary Recommendation: `compiler fix` Round (+ 1-Line `harness fix`)\\n396\\t\\n397\\tWe recommend dispatching a **`compiler fix` round** on `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` (paired with a tiny **`harness fix`** on `test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1946`), **not** raising the `2,000,000` acceptance budget:\\n398\\t\\n399\\t1. **Compiler Lowering Optimization (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`)**:\\n400\\t   - **Direct / pre-admitted intra-unit call fast path or token-forwarded non-tail outcome lane**: Top-level `defn` / `defn-` bindings compiled within the same `compile-program` unit (when not shadowed by locals) have statically known descriptors/private bodies, or non-tail admitted calls can pass `{:clj/outcome-token dsg__call_token}` (or invoke the private `av` closure directly for unshadowed intra-unit `defn`s while preserving full §8.10 descriptor publication for first-class values and cross-boundary calls).\\n401\\t   - **Streamline `dsg__assoc` / `dsg__admitted?`** for dynamic first-class descriptor calls (avoiding 7-arg nested `[k v]` vector-conj chains when native `assoc` is unshadowed, and avoiding redundant map allocations).\\n402\\t   - **Expected Impact**: Cutting intra-unit per-call cost even halfway back toward `:arg-vector` (`538 -> ~60–100` semantic steps, `934 -> ~110–180` walker steps) reduces `:check-accepted` from `2.09M -> ~0.25M–0.40M` walker steps and `:check-assume-have-discharge` from `~8.69M -> ~0.95M–1.65M` walker steps (`~0.55M–0.95M` semantic steps) — **passing all 106 fixtures on both lanes inside the existing `2,000,000` budget** and speeding up the full gate suite ~5x.\\n403\\t2. **Harness Observability Fix (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1946`)**:\\n404\\t   - Include `:consumer v` in `run-bounded`'s exhaustion `ex-info` (`(throw (ex-info \\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\" {:lane lane :steps n :consumer v}))`) so `observer/consumer-left-by-run` preserves the exhausted VM state rather than falling back to step `0`.\\n405\\t   - Keep `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn` tracked in git (included in this branch).\\n406\\t\\n407\\t### 6.2 Contingent `budget proposal` Data (If Architect Elects a Budget Change Before/Instead of Compiler Optimization)\\n408\\t\\n409\\tPer `BRIEF-h3-1.md`, if the architect elects to unblock the gate via an acceptance-budget raise prior to compiler optimization, the required measurements are:\\n410\\t\\n411\\t- **Measured Completion Costs (Instrumented Gate Mode)**:\\n412\\t  - `:check-accepted`: **`1,207,270`** (`:c-semantic`), **`2,086,120`** (`:c-walker`).\\n413\\t  - `:check-assume-have-discharge`: **`5,030,283`** (`:c-semantic`), **`~8,692,000`** projected (`:c-walker`, bounded to **`8,682,000 – 8,705,000`** by the `1.7277x – 1.7280x` walker/semantic invariant and `94.03%` call completion at `8,000,000` steps).\\n414\\t- **Measured Instrumentation Overhead**: **`+0.28%` to `+0.38%`** (`+6.00` semantic / `+11.00` walker steps per traced kernel call; `+4,330` to `+14,170` total steps).\\n415\\t- **Monotonic Progress Evidence**: Across `2M -> 4M -> 8M`, `:check-assume-have-discharge` advances strictly forward through the finite proof script (`459 -> 1,120 -> 2,219` of `2,360` calls on `:c-walker`; `927 -> 1,924 -> 2,360` halting on `:c-semantic`) with bounded continuation depth (`23 – 48` frames) and exact `A = B = C` output agreement.\\n416\\t- **Proposed Finite Bound & Headroom (Contingent Only)**:\\n417\\t  - A uniform per-lane budget would require **`12,000,000` steps** (`1.38x` headroom above `:check-assume-have-discharge` `:c-walker`'s `~8.69M` completion cost; `2.39x` above `:c-semantic`'s `5.03M`).\\n418\\t  - **Why `compiler fix` is preferred over `12,000,000`**: Raising `:instruction-budget-per-lane` to `12,000,000` leaves `95.1%–95.7%` of VM execution in avoidable per-call protocol/witness boilerplate and increases worst-case walker timeout cost `6x` (`~8.6 s -> ~52 s` per runaway lane).\\n419\\t\\n420\\t---\\n421\\t\\n422\\t## 7. Verification Record\\n423\\t\\n424\\t1. **Pre-check (`test-kernel-differential-gate`)**:\\n425\\t   - Command: `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate`\\n426\\t   - Result: `Ran 1 tests containing 661 assertions. 1 failures, 0 errors.` (`{:pass 100, :recorded-upstream-failure 2, :recorded-deviation 2, :blocked 2}`, `58` unexercised arities — only the expected `blocked` assertion fails).\\n427\\t2. **H3-0 Declarations & Evidence Round-Trip Check**:\\n428\\t   - Command: `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-acceptance-counting -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip`\\n429\\t   - Result: `Ran 2 tests containing 32 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.`\\n430\\t3. **Post-check (`test-kernel-differential-gate` & `clj-kondo`)**:\\n431\\t   - Zero changes to `src/cljc/` or `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`; post-check matches pre-check (`Ran 1 tests containing 661 assertions. 1 failures, 0 errors.`; `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`: `0 errors, 0 warnings`).\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793870000000-architect-h3-1-design-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:24:{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_5A1XDRPlDrMJQ9VGAbINAqIF\",\"content\":\"1\\tdiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\n2\\tindex 6259328b..d7f76afe 100644\\n3\\t--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\n4\\t+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\n5\\t@@ -1053,10 +1053,13 @@\\n6\\t \\n7\\t \\n8\\t (defn- call-entry\\n9\\t-  \\\"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body.\\\"\\n10\\t+  \\\"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body.\\n11\\t+   A truthy second argument selects the unit's private intra-unit lane,\\n12\\t+   where `invocation` is already the positional argument vector.\\\"\\n13\\t   []\\n14\\t   (let [body (symbol (str reserved-prefix \\\"body\\\"))\\n15\\t         invocation (symbol (str reserved-prefix \\\"invocation\\\"))\\n16\\t+        direct? (symbol (str reserved-prefix \\\"direct\\\"))\\n17\\t         outcome (symbol (str reserved-prefix \\\"entry_outcome\\\"))\\n18\\t         positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\\n19\\t         named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\\n20\\t@@ -1082,18 +1085,22 @@\\n21\\t                                        (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/thrown)\\n22\\t                                               (u/app (u/v 'data/nth)\\n23\\t                                                      (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))))))\\n24\\t-        ;; The private lane forwards the body's outcome in tail position.\\n25\\t-        ;; The public entry still converts outcomes to value/raise normally.\\n26\\t-        entry (u/lam [invocation]\\n27\\t+        ;; The private lanes forward the body's outcome in tail position.\\n28\\t+        ;; The public 1-arg entry nil-fills `direct?` and converts outcomes\\n29\\t+        ;; to value/raise normally unless authenticated by `:clj/outcome-token`.\\n30\\t+        entry (u/lam [invocation direct?]\\n31\\t                      (u/if-node\\n32\\t-                       (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\\n33\\t-                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation)\\n34\\t-                                     (u/lit :clj/outcome-token))\\n35\\t-                              (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\\n36\\t-                       (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\\n37\\t-                                  (u/app (u/v body) positional)\\n38\\t-                                  binding-error)\\n39\\t-                       entry-body))]\\n40\\t+                       (u/v direct?)\\n41\\t+                       (u/app (u/v body) (u/