ec, latte-kernel.norm/install-unfold-implicit! install-unfold-implicit, latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser! register-unparser, latte-kernel.defenv/local-definitions local-definitions, latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition register-definition, latte-kernel.unparser/prod-impl-unparser prod-impl-unparser}\\n457\\t :program-status :execution-evidence-incomplete\\n458\\t-:counts {:pass 100, :recorded-upstream-failure 2, :recorded-deviation 2, :blocked 2}\\n459\\t+:counts {:pass 102, :recorded-upstream-failure 2, :recorded-deviation 2}\\n460\\t :adaptation-version {:context 2, :kernel-assembly 4}\\n461\\t :binding-dispositions {:admitted 146, :excluded 9}\\n462\\t :upstream-revision \\\"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\\\"\\n463\\t :manifest-functions 147\\n464\\t :fresh-supply-convention {:input {:counter 0}, :allocation (gensym supply prefix), :result [symbol next-supply], :rebuild-type-result [original-result next-context], :ambient-prefix-only :refused}\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793870000000-architect-h3-1-design-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:219:{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_m77i7wNfS4IGZSXQOyZ5Anok\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Slice 9 kernel differential gate: execution evidence correction\\n2\\t\\n3\\tThe gate on the hardening line is **blocked**. The architect denied the prior\\n4\\t165/165 closure claim because membership in a static dependency closure did\\n5\\tnot prove execution of every arity. That claim is withdrawn. The gate retains\\n6\\tits final assertion `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))`; missing execution\\n7\\tevidence must fail that assertion.\\n8\\t\\n9\\tThe 106-fixture corpus has **100 passing agreements, two recorded deviations\\n10\\t(`elab-after-qed`, `check-after-qed`), two blocked fixtures, and two recorded\\n11\\tupstream failures.** The four narrowly recorded exception dispositions remain\\n12\\tdeclared departures, not agreements. No upstream or `src/cljc/` source changes\\n13\\tare made by H3-0. Admission is unchanged: 155 bindings (146 admitted, 9\\n14\\texcluded) and 175 candidate function/arities (165 admitted, 10 excluded).\\n15\\t\\n16\\tRecorded executions establish **107/165** admitted arities: 39 directly\\n17\\tand 68 through named integrations. The other **58**, including `parse/1`,\\n18\\tremain uncredited. The declared departures are carried by the versioned\\n19\\t[`slice9_declarations.edn`](slice9_declarations.edn) (provenance `ea18c8e4^`),\\n20\\trevalidated on every refresh by the representation-aware classifier: the\\n21\\tguest `:meta` value may be a pre-adoption raw closure or the admitted §8.10\\n22\\tdescriptor; structurally invalid descriptors and any payload, message, script\\n23\\tor call mismatch refuse (descriptor authenticity itself is the compiler's\\n24\\tadmission witness upstream of the outcome). The corrected counts and remaining arities\\n25\\tare recorded in [`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn) and\\n26\\t[`slice9_unexercised.edn`](slice9_unexercised.edn). The residual consumers in\\n27\\t[`fixture_closure.edn`](fixture_closure.edn) retain their concrete expected\\n28\\toutcomes; they do not establish closure of the full inventory, and their\\n29\\tcount (20) predates the re-derivation — the live unexercised set is the\\n30\\t58-name list.\\n31\\t\\n32\\t## Consumer evidence\\n33\\t\\n34\\t- `mkenv` preserves a nonempty global environment and creates empty locals.\\n35\\t- `beta-red`, `delta-normalize`, and `delta-normalize-local` have explicit\\n36\\t  entry fixtures and missing-reference rejections. The local wrapper also\\n37\\t  exercises explicit local definitions and their precedence over an ambient\\n38\\t  namespace definition.\\n39\\t- `install-unfold-implicit!` installs into both isolated upstream atoms on A.\\n40\\t  B/C return an updated immutable context, used by both the delta wrapper and\\n41\\t  NBE. Both normalizers read the same installed extension. An installed\\n42\\t  refusing extension propagates its original error data.\\n43\\t- `install-opacity-function` starts from a refusing policy, explicitly installs\\n44\\t  the working policy, then enters the original proof dispatcher through\\n45\\t  opaque/transparent steps and qed. A duplicate opaque step rejects. A uses\\n46\\t  an isolated namespace and host-local Var policy; B/C thread immutable\\n47\\t  definition updates through the explicit context.\\n48\\t- `install-fundamental-unparsers!` starts from an empty registry, installs the\\n49\\t  fundamental product unparser, then unparses nested implications. Dependent\\n50\\t  products and atoms remain unchanged. Direct `prod-impl-unparser` fixtures\\n51\\t  also verify its `[term false]` refusal result.\\n52\\t- `exists-kw?`, `term?`, `pair?`, and `vectorn?` include false results.\\n53\\t  `bound-vars` distinguishes a bound occurrence from entirely free variables.\\n54\\t  These fixtures preserve upstream behavior, including its shallow term\\n55\\t  validator and the use of `vector` rather than `vector?` in utility predicates.\\n56\\t- `proper-type?` enters each arity separately. Unknown variables throw;\\n57\\t  a well-typed term whose inferred type is not a sort returns false.\\n58\\t- `show-deftype` checks definition, axiom, theorem, implicit, and unknown\\n59\\t  labels. It depends only on portable record-kind predicates and returns a\\n60\\t  string. Host pprint and stdout functions remain excluded.\\n61\\t- `safe-get` covers successful lookup, missing keys, stored false, and stored\\n62\\t  nil. The latter three all reject upstream. `vremove` removes every match,\\n63\\t  preserves a no-match vector, and propagates a predicate's domain exception.\\n64\\t\\n65\\t`mkenv`, `appify`, and `bound-vars` have no domain rejection in the pinned\\n66\\tsource; the fixtures preserve their constructor, empty-input, and empty-set\\n67\\tresults instead of manufacturing refusals. A refused product rewrite is\\n68\\tidentified by its explicit modification flag, not mistaken for an exception.\\n69\\t\\n70\\tThe pinned local delta wrapper has a narrower portability scope than its\\n71\\tdocstring suggests: `delta-step` drops `local?` when calling `delta-reduction`\\n72\\ton a reference. Consequently upstream can resolve a global or host namespace\\n73\\tdefinition on that path. The global-result fixture preserves this behavior;\\n74\\tthe namespace fixture supplies a local definition that shadows the ambient\\n75\\tone. The guest boundary still requires explicit definitions and has no host\\n76\\tnamespace lookup capability. This round does not repair upstream or claim\\n77\\tagreement for ambient-only resolution.\\n78\\t\\n79\\t## Acceptance counting\\n80\\t\\n81\\tEvery selected guest function body appends `[guest-function arity]` to an\\n82\\texplicit diagnostic stream at entry. Instrumentation covers all arities of\\n83\\tthe functions supplied to each fixture, including higher-order calls through\\n84\\tregistries and extension closures. Each C lane creates its own stream.\\n85\\tAfter the VM halts, the harness reads that stream through its own\\n86\\tcursor, preserving the fixture's original outcome and exception payload.\\n87\\tA/B remain uninstrumented. Raw ordered call records are retained under\\n88\\t`:c-walker :executed-calls` and `:c-semantic :executed-calls` for every completed\\n89\\tfixture. The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions per\\n90\\tlane. The instrumented fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound because\\n91\\tbody-entry stream writes add guest instructions. Reading the completed\\n92\\tdiagnostic stream is harness work after halt. This is an instrumentation\\n93\\tbudget change, not a new performance acceptance claim.\\n94\\t\\n95\\tPassing direct fixtures contribute only their original function/argument\\n96\\tcount, and only with matching body-entry records in both C lanes. Passing\\n97\\tnamed integrations contribute only exact arities recorded in both C lanes.\\n98\\tStatic dependency membership contributes no credit. Full branch coverage is\\n99\\tnot required. Context adapter identities and explicit extra context arguments\\n100\\tare recorded in the evidence; each observed guest arity is checked against\\n101\\tthat mapping individually, never against all arities of its function.\\n102\\t\\n103\\tOnly `:pass` fixture rows contribute exercise evidence. Recorded upstream\\n104\\tfailures and deviations do not contribute. Any admitted arity without a\\n105\\tpassing direct or named integration execution path blocks the gate.\\n106\\t\\n107\\tThe accounting regression first failed against the old implementation: it\\n108\\tcredited the deliberately uncalled arity and accepted missing C-lane traces.\\n109\\tIt now requires both traces and leaves unused arities uncredited. A second\\n110\\tregression replaces the adapted `parse/1` body in memory with an unconditional\\n111\\terror, then runs `:parse-to-normalize-to-type`. A/B and both C lanes still\\n112\\tpass; both C traces record `parse/2` and no `parse/1`, and the counter leaves\\n113\\t`parse/1` uncredited. Every credited path is also checked against the recorded\\n114\\texecutions of its named fixture. See\\n115\\t[`slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt`](slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt).\\n116\\t\\n117\\t## Recorded portability boundaries\\n118\\t\\n119\\tThe two `:recorded-deviation` rows remain `:elab-after-qed` and\\n120\\t`:check-after-qed`. Upstream embeds `clojure.core/meta`, a host function, in\\n121\\texception data; C carries a guest closure. The original outcomes, comparison\\n122\\tflags, exact payload guards, and evidence pointers remain intact. Both rows\\n123\\tare listed in `:recorded-portability-boundaries` in the summary. Neither is\\n124\\treported as agreement.\\n125\\t\\n126\\t## Recorded upstream failures\\n127\\t\\n128\\t`:typing-ascription` still reaches the upstream declaration\\n129\\t`type-of-ascribe`, which has no definition. A raises its original unbound-fn\\n130\\texception; B/C retain the explicit branch-local refusal.\\n131\\t\\n132\\t`:compile-malformed` still passes scalar proof input `[42]`. A/B raise the\\n133\\toriginal native sequence exception; C retains its portable sequence refusal.\\n134\\t\\n135\\tThese two rows have the distinct disposition `:recorded-upstream-failure` and\\n136\\tare listed in `:recorded-upstream-failures`. Their original A/B/C records and\\n137\\tfalse agreement flags remain available. The disposition checks the exact\\n138\\tfixture ID, input call, exception class/message, B outcome, and both completed\\n139\\tC outcomes. Changed calls, IDs, or C payloads are tested to refuse the\\n140\\tdisposition. Any other execution failure remains a blocker. No upstream fix,\\n141\\taccepted-negative claim, or equality projection is introduced for these rows.\\n142\\t\\n143\\t## Verification\\n144\\t\\n145\\tAn independent audit re-derives the credited arities and fixture paths from\\n146\\tthe two raw C traces. Kondo reports zero errors and warnings. The full oracle\\n147\\truns 26 tests and 1,697 assertions with exactly one failure and no errors:\\n148\\tits retained `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` closure assertion. The\\n149\\tunexercised arities — **58** under the current accounting, including\\n150\\t`parse/1` — therefore continue to block acceptance. Verification results are\\n151\\trecorded in [`slice9_verification.edn`](slice9_verification.edn), with command\\n152\\toutputs beside it.\\n153\\t`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!` explicitly regenerates\\n154\\tboth execution evidence and the remaining-arity inventory; normal tests do\\n155\\tnot write them. Evidence retains the pinned upstream revision, compiler\\n156\\tdigest, runtime, instruction budget, per-fixture outcomes, diagnostic traces,\\n157\\tdependency graph, admission inventory, credited paths, and all four recorded\\n158\\texception dispositions.\\n159\\t\\n160\\tThe append-only correction in [`known-gaps.md`](../../../docs/agents/known-gaps.md)\\n161\\trecords that host Clojure turns a thrown string into `ClassCastException`,\\n162\\tcaught by `catch Exception` but not `catch ExceptionInfo`. Portable `try` binds\\n163\\tthe error payload without equivalent runtime class handling; this guest/host\\n164\\tgap remains declared.\\n165\\t\\n166\\tExecution scope is both C evaluators on the JVM. This correction does not\\n167\\tclaim renewed architect sign-off or Node/Dart verification, and the blocked\\n168\\tgate does not authorize program closure or merge.\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793870000000-architect-h3-1-design-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:221:{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_fvEUVzhmJLEXgPptqml6u9GH\",\"content\":\"orchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:5:Prior logs (historical claims, never appended): orchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md,\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11216:IN FLIGHT at handoff (do not kill; check, they may have finished): (a) opus AD-2 in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad2 (branch admission-ad2, UNCOMMITTED): deletes `principal-admission` and the legacy `:admit` hook, DHT import tests compose `:admission`, renames the foreign-principal test to an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm-test, adds allow and second-publisher head-change cases; brief collab/1792250000000-engineer-ad2.prompt.md, log collab/1792250000000-engineer-ad2.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log, report to datomworld-ad2/collab/1792250000000-engineer-ad2.findings.md; waits on codex review then ff master. The DHT import artifact must stay unchanged. (b) fable round 2 of the admission-in-linker design: collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md (brief collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.prompt.md); round 1 (collab/1792260000000-architect-admission-in-linker.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md) was REJECTED by codex (collab/1792261000000-reviewer-admission-in-linker.findings