\\\"two encodings\\\" assertion keeps its meaning with the reversed-row encoding; the five currently red `stage-e-rows-test` cases: `row-1-candidates-and-encodings-test`, `row-7-failure-lower-and-lost-authority-test`, `row-3-reclaim-test`, `fork-per-host-test`, `row-5-replay-divergence-test` fail only because the world supplies no source index); `stage_e_peer.cljc`, `stage_e_process_test.clj`, `stage_e_rows_test.cljc` only if needed (the Node peer build picks up the new namespaces: check the Node peer entry namespace list/regexp and update it if it names old fixtures). Acceptance (plan 7d): `stage_e_rows_test` green on JVM (slow tier with `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`), and written so it runs on Node and Dart; `stage_e_process_test` JVM-driven over `[[:jvm :jvm] [:jvm :node] [:node :jvm] [:node :node]]` with every cut a SIGKILL: you CANNOT run it fully: run the fast-lane gate `the-cross-host-handoff-across-processes-test` on the JVM pair if your sandbox allows processes and report; the orchestrator runs the Node/process matrix on shiva and jupiter. Row 10's canonical-byte agreement across hosts holds for packs (sorted rows): keep or add the assertion. All of `yin.vm.ucf.*` green after this slice (list anything red). Also land F1, F2. Portability: `.cljc` JVM/Node/Dart (no `for` over possibly long seqs, no private var access, `(assoc {} ...)`, no unary minus on floats, `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` order, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`, no EDN strings with whitespace before closers). If the plan and the code disagree, the code wins: report desig[...truncated]\\ncollab/yang-python/1792390000000-reviewer-safepoint-s3-gate.deepseek-flash.findings.md:11:The reduction adds `(count (filter #{\\\\newline \\\\return} text))` per NEWLINE token. The pinned lexer rule (`antlr/python3/Python3Lexer.g4:101`) is `NEWLINE: ({atStartOfInput}? SPACES | ('\\\\r'? '\\\\n' | '\\\\r' | '\\\\f') SPACES?)`, and `cst/token-record` exports raw `getText`. So a CRLF token `\\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\"` advances the line by **2** and a form-feed token `\\\"\\\\f\\\"` by **0**. The design amendment (`yang.antlr.md:1714`) and the function's own docstring both say \\\"the line breaks\\\", so `f_lineno` and every line event are wrong for CRLF or form-feed sources. No fixture exercises this (all use LF). Fix: increment once per NEWLINE token whose text contains `\\\\newline`, `\\\\return` or `\\\\formfeed` (the start-of-input SPACES alternative stays 0), and add CRLF + form-feed coverage.\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791304928887-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10b-kernel-lift-lower.dispatched.prompt.md:28:(1791262500000-reviewer-d10-fix-round-gate.findings.md — its findings\\ncollab/yin-vm/1792530000000-engineer-7e-docs.prompt.md:3:Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e`, branch `srvm-phase7e` from the integration branch `srvm-phase7` (7a, 7b, 7c merged; 7d is in review on branch srvm-phase7d, its facts are in `collab/1792500000000-engineer-7d-stage-e.report.md`). DOCS ONLY: edit nothing under `src/` or `test/`. Edit ONLY: `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`, `docs/orchestrator-log.md` is NOT yours (the other orchestrator owns it; put your log text in your report instead), and your report `collab/1792530000000-engineer-7e-docs.report.md`. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3: cursor (immutable dao.stream value), cursor cell (the carrier's box, `:yin.k/cc-<n>`), cursor-ref (the sealed ref a program holds), cell (the heap box only). Read: `collab/phase7-plan.md` (3.1-3.9 and the slice sections), `collab/7a-report.md` (D3 doc amendment list and codex 7a review `collab/7a-review.md` if present), the 7b and 7c reports, `collab/7c-review.md`, the 7d report, and READ THE CODE so every sentence is true: `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{rows,rows/checkpoint,handoff,holder/export,holder/driver,compose}.cljc`. Owner rulings that bind the text: fork custody slot is nil; REPL cust