itted string display-bearing | candidate slice: widen the escaping in `render.cljc` | yang.python seat | recorded by the deepseek v4 gate, confirmed against CPython 3.9.6 | P3 |\\n+| `yin.vm.values` hashes a `Continuation`/`Closure` payload recursively (`values.cljc:99`, `(:continuation owner payload)`), so hashing a deep VM state overflows the JVM stack: `StackOverflowError` in `APersistentVector.hasheq`/`Murmur3.hashUnordered`, reaching `Continuation.hasheq` and `Closure.hasheq`. Surfaces as `yang.python.antlr.safepoint-test/recursion-error-test`, `linked-safepoint-test/linked-recursion-error-test` and two `e2e-test` recursion tests. Verified identical on shiva AND jupiter at 6d6b7e71 (19/141 + 1 error; 10/51 + 1 error; 42/714 + 2 failures), and present at the PARENT commit 3ab1c925 for safepoint-test; environment-sensitive (the same tests are green on the macOS dev machine at 19/144, 10/53, 42/714) `| bound the hash depth or hash a stable identity instead of the payload; needs a stack-size boundary decision `| yin.vm (value hashing) — NOT yang.python; the Python frontend only surfaces it `| found while closing the yang.python link reds (6d6b7e71); the four link-refusal namespaces were fixed, these three were not and are out of the Python seat's scope | P2 |\\n+| Refinement of the row above, with the decisive assertion text: the Python recursion guard does not fire before the JVM stack gives out. `yang.python.antlr.e2e-test/recursion-under-real-hooks-test` (e2e_test.clj:819) expects `#:py{:exception {:type \\\"RecursionError\\\", :args [\\\"maximum recursion depth exceeded\\\"]}}` and gets `[:thrown \\\"java.lang.StackOverflowError\\\"]`. Reproduced on jupiter (independent host, no other lane) and shiva at 6d6b7e71; green on the macOS dev machine. The safepoint/linked-safepoint variants surface the same exhaustion inside `Continuation.hasheq` while hashing the state. So the three remaining yang.python slow reds are ONE root: the guest recursion depth the limit allows exceeds what a default JVM thread stack sustains on Linux `| CLOSED 2026-11-02 (6fae7fbe): the JVM default `ThreadStackSize` is 2048 KB on macOS and 1024 KB on Linux, and the guest code runs on a CREATED thread (raising `ulimit -s` to 64 MB does not help; `-J-Xss32m` makes the failing test pass 1/5/0 on jupiter). Run the affected JVM test lanes with an explicit `-Xss` of at least 2 MB, or make the guard measure remaining stack instead of a fixed depth; done — the `:test` alias now carries `:jvm-opts [\\\"-Xss4m\\\"]`, and every JVM lane inherits it `| yin.vm (recursion guard / thread stack) with the yang.python e2e evidence `| refinement found while verifying the link-reds landing (the engineer's macOS-green counts do not reproduce on Linux) | P2 (closed 2026-11-02: all seven namespaces green on Linux) |\\n | `dht-import-test` fails on Node and Dart: the test's own publication differs from the JVM artifact in the `:importers` key — the C4 publication area, JVM passes (surfaced by the C3 completion run, not a C3 detector) | diagnosis slice | yang.python seat | found at the C3 completion gate (fable: real red lane, outside C3) | P2 |\\n | `vm-rebuild-is-a-new-process-test` (yin.repl.python-antlr-test) fails on Node and Dart — expected `:register`, got `:semantic` (the VM-type default); JVM passes (surfaced by the C3 completion run, not a C3 detector) | diagnosis slice | yang.python seat | found at the C3 completion gate (fable: real red lane, outside C3) | P2 |\\n | `(compile ...)` under `:yang.python/antlr` returned an EMPTY string on Node/Dart and dumped the whole prelude (24.8M chars, ~15 s) on the JVM — pre-existing (existed under `(lang :yang.python/antlr)`), made reachable via `(lang :python)` by the legacy retirement (5308e7cf) | closed 2026-10-18 at compile-investigation (b8dbeabf + dbe1d14b + fbfb82b6): the JVM dump was the preview lowering against a nil frontend-session (the whole prelude embedded, rendered four times — now lowered :primed); the Node/Dar