ut malformed state on disk, start with `--no-state`, assert success and byte-identical state afterward | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:120:| yang.clojure: multi-arity `defn` and `fn` were deferred from slice 3 because a Yin closure nil-fills missing arguments and drops extras, so it cannot observe its call's argument count | architect session 8c1f0b7e (yang-slice3 sign-off), glm-5.3 review of yang-slice3 | yang.clojure | resolved-by-3b: opt-in argument-vector convention at `compile-program` (`:convention :arg-vector`), dispatch on `data/count` / `data/nth`, oracle legs `defenv/register-definition` (both arities, both placements) agree with upstream | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:121:| yang.clojure: destructuring lowers through the bare primitives `first`, `rest`, `empty?`; the compile-time refusal covers local bindings only, so a store `(def first ...)` or a runtime initial-`:env` entry named `first`/`rest`/`empty?` captures identically through `engine/resolve-var` (env, then store, then primitives) and is invisible to it | architect session 8c1f0b7e, glm-5.3 review of yang-slice3 | yang.clojure | open: a module-qualified alias for the core primitives (a VM-side registration question) or a refusal of top-level definitions of the three names | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:122:| yang.clojure: a destructured `&` remainder is a vector (the VM `rest` contract), where Clojure yields a seq or list; consumers that observe the shape (`list?`, `seq?`-sensitive printing) differ | architect session 8c1f0b7e ratified departure, `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` `nthnext-form` | yang.clojure | slice 7 (Clojure-compatible sequence operations) | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:123:| yang.clojure: variadic fn parameters (`[a & r]` at the top level of `fn` / `defn`) are rejected explicitly, also under the argument-vector convention | architect session 8c1f0b7e, corpus defines no variadic function | yang.clojure | slice 7 (the convention extends to variadic guest functions) | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:124:| yang.clojure: under :arg-vector, a store-level `(def conj ...)`/`(def get ...)` inside one program unit captures the convention's bare conj/get operators (resolve-var puts store ahead of primitives); engineer-verified: `(defn conj ([] [9 9]))` makes `(g 1 2)` return [9 9]; the compile-time locals check does not cover defs; architect disposition 1793206800000: ledger row, closing route = refuse top-level def of conj/get/first/rest/empty? under the convention in slice 5; cross-unit case covered by the store-shadowing row above | slice 3b review (glm session 79d4df98, verified against engine.cljc:129-132); architect sign-off fable 8c1f0b7e | yang.clojure | slice 5 (convention code touched there) | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:125:| yang.clojure: the ::defined scan in program-env reads only top-level heads, so a nested `(defn + ...)` inside do/if dispatches native while the store holds a convention closure — silent wrong result on the supported surface; architect disposition: ledger row, closing route = refuse non-top-level def under the convention, added when slice 4 registers loop/recur as special forms | slice 3b review (glm session 79d4df98, traced example (+ [1 2]) -> [:pair 1 2] not :one) | yang.clojure | slice 4 | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:126:| yang.clojure: defmacro parameters are the one binder surface skipping check-binder!/reserved-prefix validation (consciously deferred: the (defmacro defn [& xs]) test needs &); a reserved-prefix macro param can be shadowed by a generated cursor; macros never enter the convention so impact is body-level only; architect disposition: ledger row, closing route = &-aware per-param binder check, slice 4 with the nested-def refusal | slice 3b review (glm session 79d4df98) | yang.clojure | slice 4 | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:127:| yang.clojure: value-position adapters for native primitives cap at 4 arguments (magic constant), so a variadic primitive like assoc ([3 :variadic])